## std::net — TcpListener / TcpStream class shells + Shutdown enum.
##
## Wave 2 (#06.8) — partial migration. The class identities and the
## Shutdown enum (with its tag-stability contract) now live here in
## self-hosted Riven source.
##
## Methods on TcpListener / TcpStream are NOT yet migrated — they
## still flow through the static-ctor fast path in
## `mir/lower/expr/method_call.rs` and the runtime_table mangled-name
## lookup (`TcpStream_read` → `riven_tcp_stream_read`, …). Migrating
## the methods to a class-body `lib "riven_runtime"` block requires
## removing TcpListener / TcpStream from the static-ctor carve-out
## (T#20) so the standard method-call lowering — which already honours
## c_symbol via the ffi_alias_map — can pick them up. That work is
## tracked separately.
##
## The Shutdown variant order is the load-bearing contract: tag indices
## must match `RIVEN_SHUTDOWN_{READ,WRITE,BOTH}` in
## library/runtime/net/tcp.c. The `shutdown_tag_stability` pin test
## scans this file (after Wave 2 migration) instead of stdlib/mod.rs.

class TcpListener
end

class TcpStream
end

enum Shutdown
  Read
  Write
  Both
end
